Translation patch: libsignal_protocol (module list and re-exports)

Change: under the `extraction` feature, the modules `group_cipher` and `session` and the re-exports of the store-using API are left out. The sealed-sender and storage re-exports are split so that the plain types (`Direction`, `IdentityChange`, `UnidentifiedSenderMessageContent` and the certificates) stay.
Why: Charon's hax frontend panics on the `#[async_trait]` store traits when `--start-from-pub` roots them, so the extraction leaves out the store-using layer. The protocol and crypto core does not use it.
Behaviour: unchanged in the production build, which does not enable the `extraction` feature.
Relies on: protocol-storage-store_api.patch, protocol-storage_traits-store_traits.patch, protocol-sealed_sender-store_api.patch, protocol-session_management-store_api.patch

